<BaseLayout title="Shadow Copy inventory" description="How Nova Corp retains earlier versions, tests recovery and records 30 shadow-copy objects." breadcrumbs={[{label:"NOVA-FILES01",href:"systems/nova-files01/"},{label:"Shadow Copies"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">File server / Previous Versions</div><h1>Shadow Copies</h1><p class="lead">An earlier saved version of a file can help an employee recover from a mistaken edit or deletion without restoring the whole server.</p></div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container grid-main"><article class="prose">
<h2>What are Shadow Copies?</h2><p>Windows Volume Shadow Copy Service records point-in-time versions. The public inventory contains 30 VSS objects across two volume identifiers. Nine records are marked client-accessible; not all recorded objects are available to employees. Not every VSS object is an employee-accessible Previous Version.</p>
<h2>Why keep earlier versions?</h2><h3 class="file-problem">Problem</h3><p><a href={base+"people/moyo/"}>Moyo</a> accidentally changes or deletes a file on the IT drive. Recreating the file wastes time and a full-server restore is unnecessary.</p><h3 class="file-solution">Solution</h3><p>IT configured Shadow Copies so an employee can open Previous Versions, choose a recovery point from before the mistake, inspect the document and copy back only the version needed. Nova Corp's D: Shadow Copies are scheduled at 07:00 and 12:00.</p>
<Files01DocumentImages ids={["shadow-copy-two-triggers","shadow-copy-created"]}/>
<h2>How the recovery was tested</h2><ol><li>Create a disposable test file through the employee-facing Z: drive and create a snapshot.</li><li>Modify the live file, capture the modified version in a later snapshot, then delete the live file.</li><li>Open Z: Properties → Previous Versions, select a recovery point and inspect the historical file.</li><li>Copy only the file back and recheck its contents.</li></ol>
<pre><code>{'Test-Path "Z:\\CR010-Shadow-Recovery-Test.txt"\nGet-Content "Z:\\CR010-Shadow-Recovery-Test.txt"'}</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> False after deletion; True and the selected historical version's contents after copying it back.</p><p><strong>Actual:</strong> The journal records False before recovery and True with the captured modified version after recovery. A one-hour difference between server and client display times was traced to timezone presentation, not missing recovery data.</p>
<Files01DocumentImages ids={["shadow-copy-previous-it"]}/>
<p>A later separate recovery exercise proved an earlier file version matched the original SHA-256 exactly while the modified live file had a different hash. <a href={base+"reference/explore/files/SHADOW_COPY_RECOVERY/"}>Read the full recorded comparison and test details →</a></p>
<h2>View the recorded recovery points</h2><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/files/VSS/"}>Open the complete recorded VSS object inventory and limits →</a></p>
<details><summary>Technical checks · read-only verification</summary><p>These are inspection commands, not a new test or a live result.</p><h3>Inspect data-volume snapshots</h3><p><strong>Run on:</strong> NOVA-FILES01 (elevated terminal)</p><pre><code>vssadmin list shadows /for=D:</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> Existing snapshots appear for D: when retained; the client-accessible flag and actual Previous Versions availability need separate checks.</p><h3>Verify employee-visible versions</h3><p><strong>Run on:</strong> NOVA-CLIENT using an authorized account. Open the department folder’s Properties → Previous Versions.</p><p><strong>Expected:</strong> Available client-accessible versions, if retained; inspect a disposable file before any recovery.</p></details><h2>Recovery limits and related tests</h2><p>These objects are not 30 independently tested restores. Storage is shared with the underlying lab; Previous Versions are not an independent off-site backup.</p><p><a href={base+"files/backup/"}>Separate Windows Server Backup →</a> · <a href={base+"incidents/backup-target-unavailable/"}>Controlled backup target failure →</a></p>
<h2>Engineering journals</h2><p><a href={base+"journals/NovaCorp_CR-010_DFS_and_Shadow_Copies_CORRECTED/"}>CR-010 original journal →</a> · <a href={base+"journals/CR-012_Windows_Server_Backup_and_Recovery_Journal/"}>CR-012 original recovery journal →</a></p>
</article><aside><div class="sidebox"><h3>Recorded inventory</h3><p>30 objects · two volume identifiers · 9 client-accessible records.</p><p><a href={base+"learn/shadow-copy/"}>Shadow Copies explained →</a></p><p><a href={base+"files/volumes/"}>Storage volumes →</a></p><p><a href={base+"systems/nova-files01/"}>Back to NOVA-FILES01 →</a></p></div></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
